{
  "id": "u12-l06",
  "unit": "u12-have-to",
  "title": "I want to",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**চাওয়া 'want' + -তে form = 'want to'.** You know চাই, চাও, চান. Two more forms complete the set:\n\n- আমি **চাই** · তুই **চাস** · তুমি **চাও** · সে **চায়** · আপনি **চান**\n\nWith a noun it's 'want something': **আমি চা চাই** 'I want tea'. With a -তে form it's 'want to do': **আমি চা খেতে চাই** 'I want to have tea'.\n\nAs with পারা, the person stays **আমি / সে**, never the -কে form. 'Don't want to' = **চাই না**: **আমি যেতে চাই না**.\n\n**হতে** 'to become': **সে ডাক্তার হতে চায়** 'She wants to become a doctor'.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "chay",
      "bn": "চায়",
      "tr": "chay",
      "en": "he/she wants"
    },
    {
      "id": "chash",
      "bn": "চাস",
      "tr": "chash",
      "en": "you (intimate) want"
    },
    {
      "id": "shikhte",
      "bn": "শিখতে",
      "tr": "shikhte",
      "en": "to learn",
      "notes": "Infinitive of শেখা; the stem is শিখ-. বাংলা শিখতে চাই \"I want to learn Bengali\"."
    },
    {
      "id": "hote",
      "bn": "হতে",
      "tr": "hote",
      "en": "to become",
      "notes": "Infinitive of হওয়া. ডাক্তার হতে চায় \"wants to become a doctor\"."
    }
  ],
